<title>UK: UK Oct jobless fall may be exaggerated - ONS.</title>
<headline>UK Oct jobless fall may be exaggerated - ONS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>A 40,800 fall in October UK unemployment may have been exaggerated by about 10,000 to 15,000 as job centres struggled with a backlog of claims following the introduction of the jobseekers allowance, the Office for National Statistics said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>But it said this distortion was purely operational and may be corrected next month .</p>
<p>The jobseekers allowance replaced unemployment benefit from October 6 and requires claimants to be actively seeking work.</p>
</text>
